==Strategy==
In order to begin, an empty bucket must be in the player's inventory. These can be obtained for free from the [[aranei bucket dealer]] nearby. It is also advisable for players to bring: 

* A high tier [[Axe#Standard axes|axe]]
* A [[log basket]] filled with high-tier [[Woodcutting#Logs|logs]] and a [[knife]] or [[fletching knife]] to create [[seeking arrow shaft]]s to reduce banking trips
* A [[Drakan's medallion]] and/or other equippable teleport for faster banking (Alternatively, players can bank using the nearby [[Aranei scout]])
* [[Lumberjack outfit]] and/or [[Forester's ration]] (if using a [[felling axe]]) for higher experience rates

Harvesting from the tree is divided into two phases: 

==== Chopping/Bleeding ====
The process starts by beginning to chop the tree. Unlike [[Bloodwood tree|Bloodwood trees]] and much like a standard tree, chopping the engorged trees only requires one click. Once a player has begun chopping, a red progress bar appears above the tree which fills as the tree is chopped. The bar will fill slowly over time as long as the player is actively chopping the tree. Progress is not reset when the player leaves {{Fact}}. Bonus progress is awarded for successful chops. Successful chops are rolled every 4 ticks and yield 165 Woodcutting XP each. Higher tier axes give better success chances for these chops. Due to this mechanic, the exact AFK time for this phase may vary. A [[crystal axe]] can fully bleed the tree in ~110 seconds on average, while a [[dragon axe]] takes ~118 seconds on average {{Fact}}.  Unlike regular Bloodwood trees, felling axes do not make a difference to woodcutting rates{{Fact}}. 

Once the progress bar is full, the tree is fully bleeding and is ready for harvesting. 

==== Harvesting/Draining ====
To harvest the bloodwood sap, the player needs to click the tree and wait for 45 seconds for their character to drain the sap into a bucket. No experience is awarded for harvesting the sap. Progress is indicated by the tree's red progress bar depleting. After the bucket is filled with bloodwood sap, there is a chance for the player to additionally receive a [[letvek in a bucket]] in a separate bucket, which must be released by clicking on it before the tree can be chopped again.

== Rewards ==
Approximately 21.8 buckets of bloodwood sap can be obtained per hour, down from the ~95 of the standard bloodwood trees. Experience rates of ~65-70k XP/hour are possible, down from the ~210k XP/hour of the standard bloodwood trees. While using a [[felling axe]], [[forester's ration]]s are consumed with every XP drop, increasing the XP gained by 10%. This effect stacks with the [[lumberjack outfit]]'s 2.5% bonus XP.

